The best and most efficient way to shuffle an array in JavaScript is using the **Fisher-Yates (also known as Knuth) Shuffle Algorithm**. It runs in $O(n)$ time complexity and ensures that every permutation is equally likely.

Here is the function:

```javascript
function shuffleArray(array) {
  // Create a copy of the array if you don't want to mutate the original
  const shuffled = [...array]; 

  for (let i = shuffled.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    // Pick a random index from 0 to i
    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));

    // Swap elements at indices i and j
    [shuffled[i], shuffled[j]] = [shuffled[j], shuffled[i]];
  }

  return shuffled;
}

// Example usage:
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8];
console.log(shuffleArray(numbers));
