---

### 1. Missing `flex-wrap` (Most Common)
By default, flex containers force all children onto a single line (`flex-wrap: nowrap`). If the items have fixed widths that exceed the container's width, they will overflow.

**Fix:**
```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap; /* Allows items to drop to the next line */
}
```

---

### 2. The `min-width: auto` Trap (Text / Image Overflow)
Flex items have a default `min-width: auto` (or `min-height: auto` in column layouts). This prevents them from shrinking smaller than their contents—such as long text, URLs, preformatted text, or images.

**Fix:** Add `min-width: 0` to the **child items**:
```css
.item {
  min-width: 0; /* Allows the item to shrink below content size */
  /* If handling long text or URLs, also add: */
  overflow-wrap: break-word; 
}
```

---

